('127.512.d.2.A',4,'During intake, a nurse also asks about allergies and current:','["pets", "hobbies", "medications", "vacations"]'::jsonb,2,'Intake includes meds.','original'),
('127.512.d.2.B',4,'During a head-to-toe assessment, a nurse notes any abnormal findings such as a rash, swelling, or:','["happiness", "humor", "hunger", "bruising"]'::jsonb,3,'Abnormal findings.','original'),
('127.512.d.2.C',3,'Vital signs include temperature, pulse, respirations, and:','["blood pressure", "height", "hair color", "shoe size"]'::jsonb,0,'Vitals.','original'),
('127.512.d.2.C',4,'Vital signs are important because changes may be the first sign that a patient''s condition is getting:','["colder only", "worse", "longer", "louder"]'::jsonb,1,'Vitals monitor status.','original'),
('127.512.d.2.D',3,'The device used to measure blood pressure is a:','["thermometer", "oximeter", "sphygmomanometer", "stethoscope"]'::jsonb,2,'BP cuff.','original'),
('127.512.d.2.D',4,'A nurse listens to heart and lung sounds with a:','["ruler", "scale", "thermometer", "stethoscope"]'::jsonb,3,'Stethoscope.','original'),
('127.512.d.2.E',3,'A normal adult resting pulse is about 60 to 100 beats per:','["minute", "week", "hour", "day"]'::jsonb,0,'Normal pulse.','original'),
('127.512.d.2.E',4,'A body temperature of 102 degrees Fahrenheit is considered a:','["dangerous cold", "fever", "low reading", "normal reading"]'::jsonb,1,'Fever.','original'),
('127.512.d.2.F',3,'The nursing process steps include assessment, diagnosis, planning, implementation, and:','["competition", "celebration", "evaluation", "vacation"]'::jsonb,2,'ADPIE.','original'),
('127.512.d.2.F',4,'In the nursing process, setting goals and choosing actions happens during:','["evaluation", "discharge", "assessment", "planning"]'::jsonb,3,'Planning.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.A',3,'Activities of daily living include basic tasks like bathing, dressing, and:','["eating", "gaming", "shopping", "driving"]'::jsonb,0,'ADLs.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.A',4,'Tasks such as managing money and cooking are called instrumental ADLs, while bathing and dressing are called:','["hobbies", "basic ADLs", "leisure", "chores only"]'::jsonb,1,'ADL types.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.B',3,'A nurse assesses a patient''s independence by observing how well the patient can do ADLs without:','["rest", "clothes", "help", "food"]'::jsonb,2,'Independence assessment.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.B',4,'The Katz Index is a tool that scores a person''s independence in:','["math", "spelling", "music", "ADLs"]'::jsonb,3,'Katz Index.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.C',3,'A nurse promotes quality of life by encouraging patients to do as much as possible for themselves, which supports their:','["independence", "dependence", "boredom", "isolation"]'::jsonb,0,'Promote function.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.C',4,'Helping a patient stay active and involved in meaningful activities supports optimal patient:','["debt", "function", "delay", "decline"]'::jsonb,1,'Function.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.D',3,'Depression and anxiety are examples of mental health disorders that can affect a person''s ability to do:','["music only", "math only", "daily activities", "art only"]'::jsonb,2,'Mental health and ADLs.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.D',4,'A patient who stops eating and bathing because of sadness may need to be screened for:','["anemia", "arthritis", "asthma", "depression"]'::jsonb,3,'Depression screening.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.E',3,'A patient with limited arm strength may need an assistive device such as a:','["reacher or grab bar", "kite", "tuba", "skateboard"]'::jsonb,0,'Assistive devices.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.E',4,'A nurse recommends a walker for a patient who has trouble with:','["reading", "balance", "tasting", "hearing music"]'::jsonb,1,'Mobility aids.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.F',3,'If a patient cannot dress independently, the nurse''s care plan should include help with:','["gaming", "cooking dinner", "dressing", "traveling"]'::jsonb,2,'Match care to deficit.','original'),
('127.512.d.3.F',4,'A therapeutic care plan for a patient who cannot feed himself would include assistance with:','["driving", "shopping", "gardening", "eating"]'::jsonb,3,'Aligned care.','original'),
('127.512.d.4.A',3,'A certification that teaches CPR and use of an AED is called basic life:','["support", "care", "style", "action"]'::jsonb,0,'BLS.','original'),
('127.512.d.4.A',4,'The American Red Cross and the American Heart Association are two organizations that offer first aid and:','["art classes", "CPR certification", "cooking classes", "flight lessons"]'::jsonb,1,'First aid certifications.','original'),
('127.512.d.4.B',3,'A nurse with first aid and CPR certification can respond more quickly during a medical crisis, known as an:','["audit", "interview", "emergency", "meeting"]'::jsonb,2,'Advantage.','original'),
('127.512.d.4.B',4,'Many employers require nurses to keep their CPR certification:','["hidden", "expired", "secret", "current"]'::jsonb,3,'Employer requirement.','original'),
('127.512.d.4.C',3,'Pressing firmly on a cut with a clean cloth is a first aid skill used to control blood loss, also called:','["bleeding", "hearing", "sleeping", "thinking"]'::jsonb,0,'Bleeding control.','original'),
('127.512.d.4.C',4,'The recommended compression rate for adult CPR is 100 to 120 per:','["second", "minute", "day", "hour"]'::jsonb,1,'CPR rate.','original'),
('127.512.d.4.D',3,'In an emergency, a nurse''s role includes assessing the patient and calling for:','["pizza", "music", "help", "lunch"]'::jsonb,2,'Emergency role.','original'),
('127.512.d.4.D',4,'In an emergency, the nurse stays calm, follows protocol, and communicates clearly with the:','["television", "stranger", "radio", "team"]'::jsonb,3,'Teamwork in emergencies.','original'),
('127.512.d.5.A',3,'Equipment used to monitor a patient''s heart rhythm is an electrocardiogram, abbreviated:','["EKG", "MRI", "CPR", "IV"]'::jsonb,0,'EKG.','original'),
('127.512.d.5.A',4,'A pulse oximeter measures the percentage of oxygen in the patient''s:','["urine", "blood", "skin tone", "hair"]'::jsonb,1,'Pulse ox.','original'),
('127.512.d.5.B',3,'Maslow''s hierarchy lists basic needs such as food, water, and rest at the:','["top", "edge", "bottom", "middle"]'::jsonb,2,'Physiological needs.','original'),
('127.512.d.5.B',4,'A nurse uses theories such as Erikson''s stages of development to understand patient needs across the:','["calendar", "menu", "budget", "lifespan"]'::jsonb,3,'Lifespan.','original'),
('127.512.d.5.C',3,'A patient lying on the back with the head lowered below the feet is in the Trendelenburg position, which is used to:','["increase blood flow to the head", "help sleeping only", "relax the legs", "help eat"]'::jsonb,0,'Trendelenburg.','original'),
('127.512.d.5.C',4,'The position with the head of the bed raised 45 to 60 degrees, often used to help breathing and eating, is:','["Trendelenburg", "Fowler''s position", "prone", "supine"]'::jsonb,1,'Fowler''s.','original'),
('127.512.d.5.D',3,'Teaching a patient and family about care at home is called patient:','["coding", "billing", "education", "scheduling"]'::jsonb,2,'Education.','original'),
('127.512.d.5.D',4,'A good way to check that a patient understood teaching is to ask the patient to explain it in his or her own:','["songs", "dances", "pictures", "words"]'::jsonb,3,'Teach-back.','original'),
('127.512.d.5.E',3,'A walker or cane that helps a patient walk safely is an example of an assistive:','["device", "menu", "diet", "wage"]'::jsonb,0,'Assistive equipment.','original'),
('127.512.d.5.E',4,'Before using a walker, a nurse checks that it is the right height for the:','["floor", "patient", "wall", "bed"]'::jsonb,1,'Fit equipment.','original'),
('127.512.d.6.A',3,'A digital patient chart is an electronic medical:','["game", "recipe", "record", "menu"]'::jsonb,2,'EMR.','original'),
('127.512.d.6.A',4,'Technology that lets a nurse scan a patient''s wristband before giving medicine helps prevent:','["games", "sleep", "music", "errors"]'::jsonb,3,'Barcode scanning.','original'),
('127.512.d.6.B',3,'A nurse can find a patient''s lab results and normal ranges in the electronic:','["health record", "phone book", "calendar", "menu"]'::jsonb,0,'Lab values.','original'),
('127.512.d.6.B',4,'Lab results outside normal ranges are called:','["averages", "abnormal values", "vitals", "recipes"]'::jsonb,1,'Abnormal labs.','original'),
('127.512.d.6.C',3,'Using devices at home that send a patient''s readings to the care team is called remote patient:','["relaxing", "dancing", "monitoring", "traveling"]'::jsonb,2,'Remote monitoring.','original')
