('127.555.d.1.C',3,'Notes written in a patient''s chart should be clear, accurate, and:','["funny", "decorated", "complete", "secret"]'::jsonb,2,'Documentation skills.','original'),
('127.555.d.1.C',4,'A chart entry should be made as soon as possible after care is given so that it is:','["artistic", "lengthy", "humorous", "timely"]'::jsonb,3,'Timely documentation.','original'),
('127.555.d.1.D',3,'A health care worker reading a technical manual for a machine should look up unfamiliar terms in a:','["glossary", "menu", "map", "comic"]'::jsonb,0,'Technical material.','original'),
('127.555.d.1.D',4,'Complex technical material is easier to understand when it is broken into smaller:','["songs", "parts", "jokes", "colors"]'::jsonb,1,'Chunking.','original'),
('127.555.d.1.E',3,'The body keeps blood sugar in a narrow range through the hormones insulin and glucagon, which helps maintain:','["infection", "fatigue", "homeostasis", "inflammation"]'::jsonb,2,'Biological process.','original'),
('127.555.d.1.E',4,'Kidneys filter blood and help maintain a stable balance of water and:','["recipes", "games", "music", "electrolytes"]'::jsonb,3,'Chemical balance.','original'),
('127.555.d.1.F',3,'A broken bone is an example of a change in body structure caused by:','["trauma", "sleep", "hunger", "laughter"]'::jsonb,0,'Trauma.','original'),
('127.555.d.1.F',4,'A chronic disease such as osteoporosis causes bones to become:','["stronger", "weaker", "longer", "colder"]'::jsonb,1,'Disease changes.','original'),
('127.555.d.1.G',3,'Vaccines are an example of disease prevention, which helps reduce health care:','["games", "fun", "costs", "gifts"]'::jsonb,2,'Cost containment.','original'),
('127.555.d.1.G',4,'A disease that spreads across many countries is a concern for global:','["sports", "fashion", "trade shows", "health"]'::jsonb,3,'Global impact.','original'),
('127.555.d.2.A',3,'The federal law that protects the privacy of patient information is the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability:','["Act", "Plan", "Code", "Rule"]'::jsonb,0,'HIPAA.','original'),
('127.555.d.2.A',4,'Under HIPAA, patient information may be shared only with people who need it for care or have the patient''s:','["guess", "permission", "curiosity", "wish"]'::jsonb,1,'Privacy rule.','original'),
('127.555.d.2.B',3,'A real-life example of a nurse who breaks confidentiality can be used as a case study of a legal and ethical:','["award", "joke", "issue", "prize"]'::jsonb,2,'Case study.','original'),
('127.555.d.2.B',4,'Giving a patient care without permission can be considered the legal wrong of:','["courtesy", "kindness", "hospitality", "battery"]'::jsonb,3,'Legal issues.','original'),
('127.555.d.2.C',3,'A nurse who begins a personal romantic relationship with a patient is crossing professional:','["boundaries", "oceans", "streets", "rivers"]'::jsonb,0,'Boundaries.','original'),
('127.555.d.2.C',4,'Accepting an expensive gift from a patient may violate professional:','["fashion rules", "boundaries", "dress codes", "traffic laws"]'::jsonb,1,'Gifts and boundaries.','original'),
('127.555.d.2.D',3,'Cleaning hands before and after touching a patient is an example of safe practice for infection:','["growth", "decor", "control", "music"]'::jsonb,2,'Safe practice.','original'),
('127.555.d.2.D',4,'Using proper lifting techniques protects both the worker and the:','["wall", "lamp", "floor", "patient"]'::jsonb,3,'Safe handling.','original'),
('127.555.d.3.A.i',3,'During patient intake, subjective data include the patient''s description of symptoms and:','["pain level", "temperature reading", "height measured", "blood pressure reading"]'::jsonb,0,'Subjective data.','original'),
('127.555.d.3.A.i',4,'A patient says, ''My stomach hurts when I eat.'' This statement is:','["objective data", "subjective data", "a lab result", "a vital sign"]'::jsonb,1,'Subjective statement.','original'),
('127.555.d.3.A.ii',3,'When collecting subjective data, the nurse also asks about the patient''s allergies and past:','["hobbies", "pets", "medical history", "vacations"]'::jsonb,2,'Subjective history.','original'),
('127.555.d.3.A.ii',4,'Asking ''From 0 to 10, how bad is your pain?'' collects subjective data using a numeric rating:','["map", "menu", "clock", "scale"]'::jsonb,3,'Pain scale.','original'),
('127.555.d.3.B.i',3,'Objective data are information the nurse can measure or observe, such as temperature and:','["pulse", "feelings", "dreams", "worries"]'::jsonb,0,'Objective data.','original'),
('127.555.d.3.B.i',4,'A nurse counts a patient''s pulse at 88 beats per minute. This is:','["subjective data", "objective data", "an opinion", "a symptom"]'::jsonb,1,'Objective measurement.','original'),
('127.555.d.3.B.ii',3,'Observing a patient''s skin color and a visible rash is collecting objective data by:','["guessing", "listening", "inspection", "tasting"]'::jsonb,2,'Observation.','original'),
('127.555.d.3.B.ii',4,'Measuring a patient''s height and weight is collecting objective data called:','["feelings", "symptoms", "subjective data", "anthropometric measurements"]'::jsonb,3,'Anthropometric.','original'),
('127.555.d.3.B.iii',3,'Recording the patient''s blood pressure, respiratory rate, and oxygen level is collecting objective data about:','["vital signs", "hobbies", "history only", "feelings"]'::jsonb,0,'Vitals.','original'),
('127.555.d.3.B.iii',4,'An oxygen saturation reading of 98 percent on a pulse oximeter is recorded as:','["an opinion", "objective data", "subjective data", "a symptom"]'::jsonb,1,'Objective.','original'),
('127.555.d.4.A',3,'A device that delivers oxygen through small prongs in the nose is a nasal:','["tent", "mask", "cannula", "hood"]'::jsonb,2,'Oxygen equipment.','original'),
('127.555.d.4.A',4,'Oxygen is a fire hazard, so oxygen therapy requires that there be no:','["blankets", "lights", "pillows", "open flames"]'::jsonb,3,'Safety.','original'),
('127.555.d.4.B',3,'Helping a patient with bathing, dressing, and toileting is care related to activities of daily:','["living", "luck", "leisure", "learning"]'::jsonb,0,'ADL care.','original'),
('127.555.d.4.B',4,'Moving a patient regularly in bed helps prevent skin breakdown and pressure:','["songs", "injuries", "games", "parties"]'::jsonb,1,'Repositioning.','original'),
('127.555.d.4.C',3,'BLS certification teaches CPR, use of an AED, and relief of choking, abbreviated:','["MRI", "EKG", "BLS", "IV"]'::jsonb,2,'BLS.','original'),
('127.555.d.4.C',4,'BLS certification is usually valid for two years and must be:','["ignored", "shortened", "hidden", "renewed"]'::jsonb,3,'Recertification.','original'),
('127.555.d.4.D',3,'Tracking all fluids a patient takes in and all fluid that leaves the body is recording intake and:','["output", "games", "music", "jokes"]'::jsonb,0,'I&O.','original'),
('127.555.d.4.D',4,'Urine, vomit, and drainage from tubes are all counted in a patient''s fluid:','["plan", "output", "history", "intake"]'::jsonb,1,'Output includes urine.','original'),
('127.555.d.5.A',3,'A resting heart rate of 150 beats per minute is outside the normal range and is considered:','["healthy", "normal", "abnormal", "average"]'::jsonb,2,'Abnormal data.','original'),
('127.555.d.5.A',4,'Comparing a patient''s values with the normal range allows the nurse to identify which findings are:','["normal only", "funny", "pleasant", "abnormal"]'::jsonb,3,'Compare data.','original'),
('127.555.d.5.B',3,'A nurse who notices a drop in a patient''s blood pressure over several readings should report the trend to the:','["provider", "vendor", "visitor", "neighbor"]'::jsonb,0,'Report trends.','original'),
('127.555.d.5.B',4,'A nurse should report abnormal findings to the appropriate personnel following facility:','["slang", "policy", "fashion", "trend"]'::jsonb,1,'Chain of reporting.','original'),
('127.555.d.5.C',3,'An abnormal finding can be a sign that a patient''s condition is:','["improving fully", "unimportant", "getting worse", "unchanged forever"]'::jsonb,2,'Significance.','original'),
('127.555.d.5.C',4,'A sudden change in a patient''s level of consciousness is a significant abnormal finding that needs:','["a joke", "no action", "a later review", "immediate attention"]'::jsonb,3,'Significant findings.','original'),
